Z||000015||olliver||11-01-2001||12:04 AM||||I do believe that my 2700 stall speed t.c. is still a lock up.  But i'm not exactly sure.  Ever since my complete performance rebuild on my '86 GT i've had one little gremlin after another.  Now i think that my lock-up solenoid has just crapped out.  I remember doing the old cruise at 100km/h and feather the break it worked when i first got the car back on the road but it's not working now.  This is the most anoying thing about a complete rebuild, working out all the little bugs.  I still have to hook up my tranny cooler.  But i think i'm going to wait until the spring.  I don't plan on driving my GT over the winter.  If you are still going to drive it over the winter I was told by my cousin's race shop not to install the tranny rad prior to winter.  With the performance rad the fluid will always stay cold and apparently it is not good for the tranny.<P>Just something to think about.||||reg||1
